+import type { Finding } from "../finding.page-type.ts"
+
+export const aPatchRefusalNamesAMissingPageThatIsOnDisk = {
+  id: "01a07357-642a-7f08-8d14-901181e8b7b5",
+  pageTypeSlug: "finding",
+  slug: "a-patch-refusal-names-a-missing-page-that-is-on-disk",
+  domainSlug: "workspace-package/seat-system",
+
+  claim:
+    "`akasha patch apply` refuses with `this call names no agent whose page a patch would be kept beside` while the drafting agent's page is on disk and indexed under the acting agent id. The recovery the refusal prescribes writes a page that is already there, so an agent obeying the message writes over sound state and an agent declining is blocked with its draft stranded. The message names a cause that is not the cause. The true cause is not known.",
+  evidence:
+    "Observed 2026-09-05 on the akasha checkout, during a twenty-lane remediation swarm under seat ryn. Reported by the lane that hit it rather than measured by ryn.\n\nThe lane was blocked with 24 of its 69 statements still to land. It checked IDENTITY rather than existence, which is what makes the report worth keeping: the page `seat-system/subagents/pages/ryn-a20376bc60b79e11e.subagent.ts` was on disk; `index/identity/subagent/slug/`, `index/path/` and `index/value/subagent.jsonl` each held it, carrying agentId `01a06c47-5b71-7000-bab3-06f11b6b9fcf--a20376bc60b79e11e`; and `ACTING_AGENT_ID` in the lane's own shell matched that string exactly. Two other lanes landed within seconds either side, so the tree was healthy at that moment.\n\nThe failure window is narrow and odd. An `akasha edit` moments earlier resolved the same page and drafted successfully. The apply that followed did not.\n\nThe lane declined to run the repair the message prescribes, on the ground that it would re-create a page that already existed on the strength of a message the lane had evidence was wrong. That judgement was right and is the behaviour worth keeping: the prescribed recovery is destructive where the diagnosis is false, and nothing in the message tells a reader the diagnosis can be false.\n\nOne suggestive datum, NOT established as the cause and recorded only so it is not lost: `.git/data/index/stamp.jsonl` named commit `366080ef` while HEAD was `f83c7e90`, so the index lagged the swarm. Whether that lag causes this refusal was not tested.\n\nA second observation, because it shows how the message misleads a reader who trusts it. Earlier the same day ryn recorded a refusal of this same family as evidence that a subagent page vanishes transiently, and wrote that down as a finding. It was wrong. A lane checked and found the page present on disk at the moment of refusal. What had happened was that ryn took the refusal's own account of its cause and recorded it as an observation. A message that misnames its cause does not merely block the agent in front of it; it gets copied into the record as fact by the agent above.",
+} as const satisfies Finding
